[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:An Unknown Goddess]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.95]Lesson 3 | 第3课
[00:02.34]An unknown goddess | 无名女神
[00:10.64]How did the archaeologists know that the statue was a goddess? | 考古学家怎么知道那尊雕像是一位女神？
[00:16.23]Some time ago, an interesting discovery was made by archaeologists on the Aegean island of Kea. | 不久之前，考古学家们在爱琴海的基亚岛上有一项有趣的发现。
[00:24.33]An American team explored a temple which stands in an ancient city on the promontory of Ayia Irini. | 一支美国考察队勘探了阿伊亚·依里尼海角上一座古代城市中的一座庙宇。
[00:32.71]The city at one time must have been prosperous, for it enjoyed a high level of civilization. | 这座古城想必一度很繁荣，因为它享有高度文明。
[00:38.98]Houses -- often three storeys high -- were built of stone. | 房子——通常有三层楼高——是用石头建造的。
[00:44.07]They had large rooms with beautifully decorated walls. | 房间很大，墙壁装饰得很漂亮。
[00:48.39]The city was even equipped with a drainage system, for a great many clay pipes were found beneath the narrow streets. | 这座城甚至还配有排水系统，因为在狭窄的街道底下发现了大量陶土管道。
[00:57.46]The temple which the archaeologists explored was used as a place of worship from the fifteenth century B.C. until Roman times. | 考古学家们勘探的这座庙宇从公元前15世纪直至罗马时代一直是祭祀祈祷的场所。
[01:07.15]In the most sacred room of the temple, clay fragments of fifteen statues were found. | 在庙宇最神圣的房间里，发现了15尊雕像的陶土碎片。
[01:14.21]Each of these represented a goddess and had, at one time, been painted. | 每一尊都代表一位女神，而且曾经上过彩。
[01:20.18]The body of one statue was found among remains dating from the 15th century B.C. | 其中一尊雕像的躯体是在公元前15世纪的遗迹中找到的。
[01:27.02]Its missing head happened to be among remains of the fifth century B.C. | 而它缺失的头颅恰巧在公元前5世纪的遗迹中发现了。
[01:32.80]This head must have been found in Classical times and carefully preserved. | 这颗头颅一定是在古罗马时代就被发现并被精心保存下来的。
[01:37.84]It was very old and precious even then. | 即使在那时，它也已非常古老而珍贵了。
[01:41.87]When the archaeologists reconstructed the fragments, they were amazed to find that the goddess turned out to be a very modern-looking woman. | 当考古学家们把这些碎片重新拼合起来时，他们惊奇地发现那位女神竟是位相貌十分摩登的女郎。
[01:51.07]She stood three feet high and her hands rested on her hips. | 她身高3英尺，双手叉腰。
[01:55.76]She was wearing a full-length skirt which swept the ground. | 她身穿一条拖地长裙。
[01:59.95]Despite her great age, she was very graceful indeed, but, so far, the archaeologists have been unable to discover her identity. | 尽管年代久远，她的确仪态优雅；不过迄今为止，考古学家们仍未能查明她的身份。
